ssion/dispatch policy explicit in input-contract.md and architecture.md, correct the prior normalizer-only recognition statement, and bump the host canonicalization component to a new documented version (gitseq-record/2) with the new composed descriptor/digest. The /1 identity has never been activated; no existing binding is rewritten. I4 must freeze accepted input bytes and compare both rejection and skip cases against the old oracle, retaining exactly the existing two exclusions. Include unknown-schema malformed/scalar/oversized payload skip, recognized bad encodings and field sets, valid boundaries, no-decision rollback, and a planted omission of each admission check. Any further substantive oracle difference needs evidence and a resolution request rather than an exclusion. Work in the existing I3 branch/head as a reported child, with its own promise/artifact; review and seal with I3. Keep all successor replay fixture-only and binding inactive. The scalar-JSON upstream defect remains separately blocking.","to":"826c05d4fd56efee52cb270debdccd04322835c8dd312ec29c01dc33a9ebe003"}}